KG42.register("source_edge_archive-aa93d76c50f9bc509c2add76",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::E::v141-c-R010-E001","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-c38847500f58498d","target":"COMP-5d6a447386335cd5","source_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade","target_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R010::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","target_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. | Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"b5a81c0b4f18990b0b5620d1d8286154f427259884be1319cf530ad0841497ba","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0 Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","target_definition":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0. A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Selling surplus energy to the MGO produces prosumer revenue p_s(E_n^g − x_n). Scope: Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0.","expression":"p_s (E_n^g - x_n)  for  E_n^g - x_n > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-ps","v141-c-R010-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"A prosumer's energy purchase from the MGO has the monetary term p_b(E_n^g − x_n), represented as negative revenue in its utility. Scope: Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","expression":"p_b (E_n^g - x_n)  for  E_n^g - x_n \u003c= 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R010-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R010-pb","v141-c-R010-Eng"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"revenue of trading energy. In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for differ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Stackelberg ESM: surplus-energy sales by a prosumer to the MGO within the microgrid. | Stackelberg ESM: the buyer branch of prosumer transactions with the MGO within the microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"paper_scope_note":"Stackelberg ESM, deviation billing, and the Cournot baseline are kept separate; buying/selling branches, numerical cases, and the no-deviation/penalty conditions are retained with the declaration."}});
